From: my-other-github-account
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] dflash converter: keep verifier-owned embedding/output tensors

The Lucebox MiniMax public repro uses an adapter-only checkpoint plus a tiny
verifier metadata directory that carries the verifier-owned shared
`model.embed_tokens.weight` and `lm_head.weight` tensors.  The served drafter
GGUF gate is byte-identical only when those two tensors are preserved in the
GGUF as:

  - token_embd.weight
  - output.weight

An older public patch dropped `embed_tokens.weight` and `lm_head.weight` as
"unused", which made the converter emit a 69-tensor adapter-only GGUF.  The
banked served-drafter artifact is 71 tensors and has md5
63cdd84c69ef6086a9d15820b866ef8b.  Do not drop the shared I/O tensors;
strip a leading `model.` prefix so verifier-meta safetensors map through the
normal tensor-name mapper, and force the explicit output head to BF16/F16 so a
mostly-quantized export path cannot accidentally quantize it.

---
 convert_hf_to_gguf.py        | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 gguf-py/gguf/constants.py    |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/convert_hf_to_gguf.py b/convert_hf_to_gguf.py
--- a/convert_hf_to_gguf.py
+++ b/convert_hf_to_gguf.py
@@ -4769,6 +4769,22 @@ class DFlashDraftModel(TextModel):
             if pattern:
                 self.gguf_writer.add_sliding_window_pattern(pattern)
 
+    def modify_tensors(self, data_torch: Tensor, name: str, bid: int | None) -> Iterable[tuple[str, Tensor]]:
+        # Verifier-meta checkpoints use Hugging Face names such as
+        # model.embed_tokens.weight.  Strip only the leading model. prefix and
+        # let the normal mapper preserve embed_tokens.weight -> token_embd.weight
+        # and lm_head.weight -> output.weight.  d2t/t2d stay absent because the
+        # public Lucebox prep script never writes them into the staged checkpoint.
+        if name.startswith("model."):
+            name = name[len("model."):]
+        yield from super().modify_tensors(data_torch, name, bid)
+
+    def tensor_force_quant(self, name: str, new_name: str, bid: int | None, n_dims: int) -> gguf.GGMLQuantizationType | bool:
+        # Keep the explicit verifier output head in a lossless type.  It is part
+        # of the md5-gated served-drafter GGUF and must not be quantized away by
+        # a mostly-quantized converter run.
+        if name == "lm_head.weight" or new_name == "output.weight":
+            return gguf.GGMLQuantizationType.F16 if self.ftype == gguf.LlamaFileType.MOSTLY_F16 else gguf.GGMLQuantizationType.BF16
+        return super().tensor_force_quant(name, new_name, bid, n_dims)
+
 
 @ModelBase.register("Qwen3MoeForCausalLM")
 class Qwen3MoeModel(Qwen2MoeModel):
diff --git a/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py b/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
--- a/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
+++ b/gguf-py/gguf/constants.py
@@ -3866,7 +3866,9 @@ MODEL_TENSORS: dict[MODEL_ARCH, list[MODEL_TENSOR]] = {
         MODEL_TENSOR.FFN_UP_SHEXP,
     ],
     MODEL_ARCH.DFLASH_DRAFT: [
+        MODEL_TENSOR.TOKEN_EMBD,
         MODEL_TENSOR.OUTPUT_NORM,
+        MODEL_TENSOR.OUTPUT,
         MODEL_TENSOR.ATTN_NORM,
         MODEL_TENSOR.ATTN_Q,
         MODEL_TENSOR.ATTN_Q_NORM,
